\subsection{Gang and Symbiotic Coscheduling Strategy}

To prevent IPC boundary stalls across multikernel partitions, Telix
enforces \textbf{Matrix Gang Coscheduling}:

\begin{description}
    \item[\textbf{Coordinated Time Slicing:}] Multikernel partitions share a synchronized hardware timer grid. High-bandwidth communication paths register a "gang capability" requirement to lock synchronous execution windows across partition boundaries.

    \item[\textbf{Symbiotic Coscheduling:}] If strict gang scheduling leaves idle CPU cycles on specific cores due to task imbalance, the local EEVDF executor backfills open execution slots with latency-insensitive background continuations that consume non-conflicting memory channels.
\end{description}
